        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-03-06T15:03:20.409Z",
        "cooked": "<p>A bugbear is another word for a Boogeyman, and the Boogeyman is a thing that mostly kids are afraid of.  I think that the big reason why Bugbear is kind of a wet noodle of a character is that he’s an R-rated character in PG-13 books; he’s the kind of person who actively likes to slaughter weak characters, which could include children (he has the card Easy Prey after all).  So if you’re not allowed to do the one thing that’s scariest about Bugbear, then Bugbear is not that scary.</p>",
